moved: Access to an object that was handed over to a thread ('fire handover').
global: A global variable belongs to the main program: an object of this thread goes there only with a word - 'copy x' (a copy) or 'take x' (moved).
field: The field 'last' of an object of the globals belongs to the main program: an object of this thread goes there only with a word - 'copy x' (a copy) or 'take x' (moved).
element: An element of an array of the globals belongs to the main program: an object of this thread goes there only with a word - 'copy x' (a copy) or 'take x' (moved).
add: 'Add' runs in the main program (an object of its globals): an object of this thread goes there only with a word - 'copy x' (a copy) or 'take x' (moved).
